{"html":"<article class=\"\"><div class=\"content-top\"><\/div><div class=\"textblock\" data-banner-type=\"no-banner\"><h1>GPIO - General Purpose Input/Output<span id=\"gpio-general-purpose-input-output\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-general-purpose-input-output\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h1><p style=\"color:inherit\">General Purpose Input/Output (GPIO) API. <\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">This module contains functions to control the GPIO peripheral of Silicon Labs 32-bit MCUs and SoCs. The GPIO peripheral is used for pin configuration and direct pin manipulation and sensing as well as routing for peripheral pin connections. <\/p><div class=\"decl-class-section\"><h2>Enumerations<span id=\"enum-declaration\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#enum-declaration\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">enum<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-type-def\">GPIO_Port_TypeDef<\/a> {<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioPortA = 0<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioPortB = 1<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioPortC = 2<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioPortD = 3<\/div><div class=\"attributename\">}<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO ports IDs. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">enum<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-mode-type-def\">GPIO_Mode_TypeDef<\/a> {<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeDisabled = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_DISABLED<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeInput = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_INPUT<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeInputPull = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_INPUTPULL<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeInputPullFilter = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_INPUTPULLFILTER<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModePushPull = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_PUSHPULL<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModePushPullAlternate = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_PUSHPULLALT<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredOr = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDOR<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredOrPullDown = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDORPULLDOWN<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAnd = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDAND<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndFilter = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDFILTER<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndPullUp = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDPULLUP<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndPullUpFilter = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDPULLUPFILTER<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternate = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDALT<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternateFilter = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDALTFILTER<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternatePullUp = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDALTPULLUP<\/div><div class=\"enum\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternatePullUpFilter = _GPIO_P_MODEL_MODE0_WIREDANDALTPULLUPFILTER<\/div><div class=\"attributename\">}<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pin mode. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"decl-class-section\"><h2>Functions<span id=\"func-declaration\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#func-declaration\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-dbg-location-set\">GPIO_DbgLocationSet<\/a>(unsigned int location)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Sets the pin location of the debug pins (Serial Wire interface). <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-dbg-swd-clk-enable\">GPIO_DbgSWDClkEnable<\/a>(bool enable)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/disable serial wire clock pin. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-dbg-swdio-enable\">GPIO_DbgSWDIOEnable<\/a>(bool enable)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/disable serial wire data I/O pin. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-dbg-swo-enable\">GPIO_DbgSWOEnable<\/a>(bool enable)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/Disable serial wire output pin. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-em4-disable-pin-wakeup\">GPIO_EM4DisablePinWakeup<\/a>(uint32_t pinmask)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable GPIO pin wake-up from EM4. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-em4-enable-pin-wakeup\">GPIO_EM4EnablePinWakeup<\/a>(uint32_t pinmask, uint32_t polaritymask)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable GPIO pin wake-up from EM4. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">uint32_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-em4-get-pin-wakeup-cause\">GPIO_EM4GetPinWakeupCause<\/a>(void)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Check which GPIO pin(s) that caused a wake-up from EM4. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-em4-set-pin-retention\">GPIO_EM4SetPinRetention<\/a>(bool enable)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable GPIO pin retention of output enable, output value, pull enable, and pull direction in EM4. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-ext-int-config\">GPIO_ExtIntConfig<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin, unsigned int intNo, bool risingEdge, bool fallingEdge, bool enable)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Configure the GPIO external pin interrupt. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-em4-wu-ext-int-config\">GPIO_EM4WUExtIntConfig<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin, uint32_t intNo, bool polarity, bool enable)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Configure EM4WU pins as external level-sensitive interrupts. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-input-sense-set\">GPIO_InputSenseSet<\/a>(uint32_t val, uint32_t mask)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/disable input sensing. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-int-clear\">GPIO_IntClear<\/a>(uint32_t flags)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clear one or more pending GPIO interrupts. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-int-disable\">GPIO_IntDisable<\/a>(uint32_t flags)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable one or more GPIO interrupts. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-int-enable\">GPIO_IntEnable<\/a>(uint32_t flags)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable one or more GPIO interrupts. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">uint32_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-enabled-int-get\">GPIO_EnabledIntGet<\/a>(void)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get enabled GPIO interrupts. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">uint32_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-int-get\">GPIO_IntGet<\/a>(void)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get pending GPIO interrupts. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">uint32_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-int-get-enabled\">GPIO_IntGetEnabled<\/a>(void)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get enabled and pending GPIO interrupt flags. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-int-set\">GPIO_IntSet<\/a>(uint32_t flags)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set one or more pending GPIO interrupts from SW. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-lock\">GPIO_Lock<\/a>(void)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Lock the GPIO configuration. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">unsigned int<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-in-get\">GPIO_PinInGet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Read the pad value for a single pin in a GPIO port. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\"><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-mode-type-def\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_Mode_TypeDef<\/a><\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-mode-get\">GPIO_PinModeGet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get the mode for a GPIO pin. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-mode-set\">GPIO_PinModeSet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin, GPIO_Mode_TypeDef mode, unsigned int out)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set the mode for a GPIO pin. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-out-clear\">GPIO_PinOutClear<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set a single pin in GPIO data out port register to 0. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">unsigned int<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-out-get\">GPIO_PinOutGet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get current setting for a pin in a GPIO port data out register. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-out-set\">GPIO_PinOutSet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set a single pin in GPIO data out register to 1. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-pin-out-toggle\">GPIO_PinOutToggle<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, unsigned int pin)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Toggle a single pin in GPIO port data out register. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">uint32_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-in-get\">GPIO_PortInGet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Read the pad values for GPIO port. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-out-clear\">GPIO_PortOutClear<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, uint32_t pins)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set bits in DOUT register for a port to 0. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">uint32_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-out-get\">GPIO_PortOutGet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get the current setting for a GPIO port data out register. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-out-set\">GPIO_PortOutSet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, uint32_t pins)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set bits GPIO data out register to 1. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-out-set-val\">GPIO_PortOutSetVal<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, uint32_t val, uint32_t mask)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set GPIO port data out register. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-port-out-toggle\">GPIO_PortOutToggle<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, uint32_t pins)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Toggle pins in GPIO port data out register. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-slewrate-set\">GPIO_SlewrateSet<\/a>(GPIO_Port_TypeDef port, uint32_t slewrate, uint32_t slewrateAlt)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set slewrate for pins on a GPIO port. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">void<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#gpio-unlock\">GPIO_Unlock<\/a>(void)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Unlock the GPIO configuration. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"decl-class-section\"><h2>Macros<span id=\"define-declaration\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#define-declaration\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-gpio-port-a\">SL_GPIO_PORT_A<\/a> gpioPortA<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Mapping between SL_GPIO_PORT_ enums and gpioPort values. <\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-gpio-port-b\">SL_GPIO_PORT_B<\/a> gpioPortB<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-gpio-port-c\">SL_GPIO_PORT_C<\/a> gpioPortC<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-gpio-port-d\">SL_GPIO_PORT_D<\/a> gpioPortD<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"def-class-section\"><h2>Enumeration Documentation<span id=\"enum-definition\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#enum-definition\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><h3>GPIO_Port_TypeDef<span id=\"gpio-port-type-def\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-port-type-def\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>GPIO_Port_TypeDef<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO ports IDs. <\/p><table><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Enumerator<\/th><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioPortA<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Port A. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioPortB<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Port B. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioPortC<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Port C. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioPortD<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Port D. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_Mode_TypeDef<span id=\"gpio-mode-type-def\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-mode-type-def\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>GPIO_Mode_TypeDef<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pin mode. <\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">For more details on each mode, refer to the reference manual. <\/p><table><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Enumerator<\/th><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeDisabled<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Input disabled. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeInput<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Input enabled. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeInputPull<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Input enabled. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeInputPullFilter<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Input enabled with filter. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModePushPull<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Push-pull output. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModePushPullAlternate<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Push-pull using alternate control. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredOr<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Wired-or output. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredOrPullDown<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Wired-or output with pull-down. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAnd<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndFilter<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output with filter. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndPullUp<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output with pull-up. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndPullUpFilter<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output with filter and pull-up. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternate<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output using alternate control. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternateFilter<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output using alternate control with filter. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternatePullUp<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output using alternate control with pull-up. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">gpioModeWiredAndAlternatePullUpFilter<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Open-drain output using alternate control with filter and pull-up. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><br><\/div><\/div><div class=\"def-class-section\"><h2>Function Documentation<span id=\"func-definition\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#func-definition\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><h3>GPIO_DbgLocationSet<span id=\"gpio-dbg-location-set\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-dbg-location-set\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_DbgLocationSet (unsigned int location)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Sets the pin location of the debug pins (Serial Wire interface). <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>unsigned int<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">location<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The debug pin location to use (0-3). <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Changing the pins used for debugging uncontrolled, may result in a lockout.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_DbgSWDClkEnable<span id=\"gpio-dbg-swd-clk-enable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-dbg-swd-clk-enable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_DbgSWDClkEnable (bool enable)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/disable serial wire clock pin. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">enable<\/td><td><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">false - disable serial wire clock. <\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">true - enable serial wire clock (default after reset). <\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disabling SWDClk will disable the debug interface, which may result in a lockout if done early in startup (before debugger is able to halt core).<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_DbgSWDIOEnable<span id=\"gpio-dbg-swdio-enable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-dbg-swdio-enable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_DbgSWDIOEnable (bool enable)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/disable serial wire data I/O pin. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">enable<\/td><td><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">false - disable serial wire data pin. <\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">true - enable serial wire data pin (default after reset). <\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disabling SWDClk will disable the debug interface, which may result in a lockout if done early in startup (before debugger is able to halt core).<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_DbgSWOEnable<span id=\"gpio-dbg-swo-enable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-dbg-swo-enable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_DbgSWOEnable (bool enable)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/Disable serial wire output pin. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">enable<\/td><td><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">false - disable serial wire viewer pin (default after reset). <\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">true - enable serial wire viewer pin. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enabling this pin is not sufficient to fully enable serial wire output, which is also dependent on issues outside the GPIO module. Refer to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/dbg#dbg-swo-enable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">DBG_SWOEnable()<\/a>.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Warnings<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">If debug port is locked, SWO pin is not disabled automatically. To avoid information leakage through SWO, disable SWO pin after locking debug port.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_EM4DisablePinWakeup<span id=\"gpio-em4-disable-pin-wakeup\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-em4-disable-pin-wakeup\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_EM4DisablePinWakeup (uint32_t pinmask)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable GPIO pin wake-up from EM4. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">pinmask<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Bit mask containing the bitwise logic OR of which GPIO pin(s) to disable. Refer to Reference Manuals for pinmask to GPIO port/pin mapping. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_EM4EnablePinWakeup<span id=\"gpio-em4-enable-pin-wakeup\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-em4-enable-pin-wakeup\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_EM4EnablePinWakeup (uint32_t pinmask, uint32_t polaritymask)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable GPIO pin wake-up from EM4. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">pinmask<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A bitmask containing the bitwise logic OR of which GPIO pin(s) to enable. See Reference Manuals for a pinmask to the GPIO port/pin mapping. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">polaritymask<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A bitmask containing the bitwise logic OR of GPIO pin(s) wake-up polarity. See Reference Manuals for pinmask-to-GPIO port/pin mapping. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">When the function exits, EM4 mode can be safely entered.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">It is assumed that the GPIO pin modes are set correctly. Valid modes are <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-mode-input\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">gpioModeInput<\/a> and <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-mode-input-pull\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">gpioModeInputPull<\/a>.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_EM4GetPinWakeupCause<span id=\"gpio-em4-get-pin-wakeup-cause\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-em4-get-pin-wakeup-cause\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t GPIO_EM4GetPinWakeupCause (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Check which GPIO pin(s) that caused a wake-up from EM4. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Bit mask containing the bitwise logic OR of which GPIO pin(s) caused the wake-up. Refer to Reference Manuals for pinmask to GPIO port/pin mapping. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_EM4SetPinRetention<span id=\"gpio-em4-set-pin-retention\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-em4-set-pin-retention\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_EM4SetPinRetention (bool enable)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable GPIO pin retention of output enable, output value, pull enable, and pull direction in EM4. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">enable<\/td><td><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">true - enable EM4 pin retention. <\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">false - disable EM4 pin retention. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">On series 0 devices EM4 gpio retention can either be turned on or off. On series 1 devices there are three EM4 GPIO retention modes available. These modes are \"Disabled\", \"EM4EXIT\" and \"SWUNLATCH\". Use the <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/emu#emu-em4-init\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">EMU_EM4Init()<\/a> to configure the GPIO retention mode on a series 1 device.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\">\nThe behavior of this function depends on the configured GPIO retention mode. If the GPIO retention mode is configured to be \"SWUNLATCH\" then this function will not change anything. If the retention mode is anything else then this function will set the GPIO retention mode to \"EM4EXIT\" when the enable argument is true, and \"Disabled\" when false.<\/p><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_ExtIntConfig<span id=\"gpio-ext-int-config\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-ext-int-config\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_ExtIntConfig (<a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-port-type-def\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_Port_TypeDef<\/a> port, unsigned int pin, unsigned int intNo, bool risingEdge, bool fallingEdge, bool enable)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Configure the GPIO external pin interrupt. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-port-type-def\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_Port_TypeDef<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">port<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The port to associate with the <code>pin<\/code>.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>unsigned int<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">pin<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The pin number on the port.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>unsigned int<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">intNo<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The interrupt number to trigger.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">risingEdge<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set to true if the interrupt will be enabled on the rising edge. Otherwise, false.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">fallingEdge<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set to true if the interrupt will be enabled on the falling edge. Otherwise, false.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">enable<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set to true if the interrupt will be enabled after the configuration is complete. False to leave disabled. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-disable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntDisable()<\/a> and <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-enable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntEnable()<\/a>. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">It is recommended to disable interrupts before configuring the GPIO pin interrupt. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-disable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntDisable()<\/a> for more information.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">The GPIO interrupt handler must be in place before enabling the interrupt.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that any pending interrupt for the selected interrupt is cleared by this function.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">On series 0 devices, the pin number parameter is not used. The pin number used on these devices is hardwired to the interrupt with the same number. <br>\n On series 1 devices, the pin number can be selected freely within a group. Interrupt numbers are divided into 4 groups (intNo / 4) and valid pin number within the interrupt groups are: 0: pins 0-3 (interrupt number 0-3) 1: pins 4-7 (interrupt number 4-7) 2: pins 8-11 (interrupt number 8-11) 3: pins 12-15 (interrupt number 12-15)<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_EM4WUExtIntConfig<span id=\"gpio-em4-wu-ext-int-config\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-em4-wu-ext-int-config\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_EM4WUExtIntConfig (<a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-port-type-def\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_Port_TypeDef<\/a> port, unsigned int pin, uint32_t intNo, bool polarity, bool enable)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Configure EM4WU pins as external level-sensitive interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-port-type-def\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_Port_TypeDef<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">port<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The port to associate with the <code>pin<\/code>.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>unsigned int<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">pin<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The pin number on the port.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">intNo<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The EM4WU interrupt number to trigger.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">polarity<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">true = Active high level-sensitive interrupt. false = Active low level-sensitive interrupt.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">enable<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set to true if the interrupt will be enabled after the configuration is complete. False to leave disabled. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-disable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntDisable()<\/a> and <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-enable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntEnable()<\/a>. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">It is recommended to disable interrupts before configuring the GPIO pin interrupt. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-disable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntDisable()<\/a> for more information.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">The GPIO interrupt handler must be in place before enabling the interrupt.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that any pending interrupt for the selected interrupt is cleared by this function.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">The selected port/pin must be mapped to an existant EM4WU interrupt. Each EM4WU signal is connected to a fixed pin. Refer to the Alternate Function Table in the device Datasheet for the location of each EM4WU signal. For example, on xG22 device, the interrupt of EM4WU6 is fixed to pin PC00.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_InputSenseSet<span id=\"gpio-input-sense-set\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-input-sense-set\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_InputSenseSet (uint32_t val, uint32_t mask)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable/disable input sensing. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">val<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Bitwise logic OR of one or more of: <\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO_INSENSE_INT - interrupt input sensing. <\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO_INSENSE_PRS - peripheral reflex system input sensing.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">mask<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Mask containing bitwise logic OR of bits similar as for <code>val<\/code> used to indicate which input sense options to disable/enable. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disabling input sensing if not used, can save some energy consumption.<\/p><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_IntClear<span id=\"gpio-int-clear\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-int-clear\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_IntClear (uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clear one or more pending GPIO interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Bitwise logic OR of GPIO interrupt sources to clear. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_IntDisable<span id=\"gpio-int-disable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-int-disable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_IntDisable (uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable one or more GPIO interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO interrupt sources to disable. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_IntEnable<span id=\"gpio-int-enable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-int-enable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void GPIO_IntEnable (uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable one or more GPIO interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO interrupt sources to enable. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Depending on the use, a pending interrupt may already be set prior to enabling the interrupt. To ignore a pending interrupt, consider using <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.3/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/gpio#gpio-int-clear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">GPIO_IntClear()<\/a> prior to enabling the interrupt.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_EnabledIntGet<span id=\"gpio-enabled-int-get\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-enabled-int-get\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t GPIO_EnabledIntGet (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get enabled GPIO interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enabled GPIO interrupt sources. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_IntGet<span id=\"gpio-int-get\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-int-get\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t GPIO_IntGet (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get pending GPIO interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">GPIO interrupt sources pending. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>GPIO_IntGetEnabled<span id=\"gpio-int-get-enabled\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#gpio-int-get-enabled\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t GPIO_IntGetEnabled (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get enabled and pending GPIO interrupt flags. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Useful for handling more interrupt sources in the same interrupt handler.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Interrupt flags are not cleared by the use of this function.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pending and enabled GPIO interrupt sources. The return value is the bitwise AND combination of<\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">the OR combination of enabled interrupt sources 